==Trivia==
*In the [[Media:Eve l 003 en.png|event poster]] for [[Bears be Bare (Monthly Event)|Bears be Bare]], this enemy is referred to as Audience Bears, which was the only name they had until they were added to the [[Enemy Guide]] in [[Version 13.3 Update|Version 13.3]].
*Their Japanese name, "Bear Talk" (クマトーク ''Kumatōku''), is most likely a reference to the comedy-focused talk show ''[[wikipedia:Ametalk!|Ametalk!]]'' (アメトーーク ''Ametōku''), as the Japanese names of the [[Bears be Bare (Monthly Event)|Bears be Bare]] and [[Bears Be Back (Monthly Event)|Bears Be Back]] stages also tend to be themed around comedy.
*This enemy's concept may be a pun based on the multiple meanings of the Japanese word ''hinadan''. The most common meaning is a tiered stand used to display ''hina-ningyō'' during ''[[wikipedia:Hinamatsuri|Hinamatsuri]]'' - the basis of the Bears be Bare event - but can also refer to tiered seats/platforms for kabuki musicians or ministers in the National Diet, which are similar to Bears Be Bare's bleachers.

